      plant: "lift",
      title: "Building elevator 5/7: two speeds and slow-down",
      brief: "Passengers want speed. Travel at <b>FAST</b> (Q0.2 together with the hoist output, 4× faster) and switch to slow speed at the <b>slow-down vane</b> before the floor where the car will stop: I3.0 is on in the last 0.35 floor <b>below</b> every floor (travelling up), I3.1 in the last 0.35 floor <b>above</b> every floor (travelling down). Stopping at full speed is a <b>hard stop</b> (counted on the machine): there must be none. A call that arrives when the car is already past the slow-down point is not served now: the car passes and comes back for it.",
