      hints: ["Watch the machine: what is the LAST thing that happened, and what should come next?", "Compare what you SEE on the machine with what the PLC SEES in the I/O table (live values). A mismatch points at the field.", "Force the signal you suspect (F in the I/O table): if the machine then works, the program is fine and you have found the faulty part."],
      options: [{"t": "The counter preset is wrong", "ok": false, "why": "The counter does not even count 1: its value stays 0 whatever the preset."}, {"t": "The photo-eye always sees something: dirty lens, or reflector knocked out of line", "ok": true, "why": "I0.2 stays 1 even with no box in front of it. A counter counts changes, and a signal that never changes is never counted."}, {"t": "The photo-eye cable is broken", "ok": false, "why": "A broken cable gives 0, never 1. The I/O table shows I0.2 = 1 with no box there."}, {"t": "The conveyor runs too fast for the sensor", "ok": false, "why": "Then some boxes would be missed, not all, and I0.2 would still go 0 between boxes."}],
